    section1Body: "The groom's session is treated as unhurried and detailed — kalgi, brooch or feather placement is checked against the sherwani — while the rest of the wedding party follows a faster, still-coordinated fold.",
    section2Title: "How to book",
    section2Body: "Booking works best when the groom, family and baraati quantities are shared separately, since each group is styled differently. Send all three together for the most accurate quote.",
